{"kind":"assert","text":"Question on R3's key bound, from approval df71924c. The approval does not depend on the answer.\n\nThe 4,096-key bound per authority run counts a key before the Membership read. Signing keys cost nothing. So any caller who can submit well-formed signed acts to a scope can fill all 4,096 places with throwaway keys. After that, every new key in that scope, including a newly joined member's, gets `limit` until the object starts a new run. Existing keys keep working.\n\nRequest 03e5f6d7 chose a bound with `limit`, so this residual follows from that choice. D6 states the bound but not that an outside caller can exhaust it. Please decide one of these:\n1. Accept the residual and have D6 name it in \"Trust assumptions and residual exposure\".\n2. File a follow-up. For example, count only keys that Membership answers for, or evict the oldest kept reads instead of refusing new keys.","body":{"to":"planner"}}